In article <1990Nov8.031321.10487@cunixf.cc.columbia.edu>, eh@cunixb.cc.columbia.edu (Erik Hilsdale) writes:
 
>         How about a new item... the bathroom scale.  Has a fixed
> number of charges (for playability... there are some things nethackers
> were not meant to know), say five or so.
 
Nonsense.  There is nothing magical about a bathroom scale.  It's a platform,
a spring, and a dial.  If you want to limit them, you could have them break 
if too much weight was placed on them ("You hear a sproing!--more--" "You 
weigh 27640 stone.").
 
If there must be charges, let them be fortunes, like you (used to) get from 
those scales you (used to) see in malls.
 
> It's a tool, of course, and you'd [a]pply it to some item in your inventory 
> and it'd return the weight of that item (surprise surprise).
 
Or, also, put it on the floor and walk onto it.  Walking onto it would say
"There is a bathroom scale here.--more--" "You weigh 100 stone.--more--" 
"You step off."  Then you could drop a thing (or things) on it.  Or maybe 
the "#sit on" command could be extended to "#sit/stand on".  Same idea.


